**v0.5.3** hardens SAGA for real field use. The player now starts from a
fresh GPS fix instead of centring on stale coordinates, preserves free map
exploration, supports a predictable compass overview/follow cycle and keeps
player tracking stable while moving.

Mission nodes now use explicit progression semantics: completed nodes are
green, the next active node is yellow with the only mission halo, and future
locked nodes are red. QR nodes retain their number and use one compact type
badge for collectible, key/requirement, clue or bonus roles.

When online routing is available, the map can request a road-following guide
between mission nodes and cache the returned geometry locally. Tools and the
offline preparation panel were also reorganized around downloading the mission
and map, saving progress, recovering connectivity and synchronizing pending
events.

The four production-ready reusable games remain Circuit Matrix, Sequence Code,
Place Mosaic and Tilt Maze. The public Git history starts at the v0.0.1
baseline; earlier private or internal iteration history is intentionally not
included.

'''
readme = readme[:start] + status + readme[end:]
readme = replace_once(
    readme,
    "- improve PWA installation, caching and offline recovery;",
    "- field-test road routing in urban and rural missions and add selectable route profiles;\n"
    "- improve PWA installation, caching and offline recovery;",
    "roadmap",
)
readme_path.write_text(readme, encoding="utf-8")

changelog_path = Path("CHANGELOG.md")
changelog = changelog_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
entry = f'''# Changelog

## {VERSION} — Offline GPS and field map release
{DATE}

- Starts the player from a fresh GPS fix and rejects stale stored coordinates for initial centring.
- Preserves free map exploration and adds a predictable compass overview/follow cycle.
- Keeps player tracking stable while new GPS readings arrive.
- Uses explicit mission-node semantics: completed green, next active yellow and locked future red.
- Restricts the animated mission halo to the next active node.
- Keeps a visible number on every node and uses one compact QR type badge without duplicate lock symbols.
- Adds a road-following mission guide through OSRM when routing is available.
- Caches road-route geometry locally and avoids drawing a misleading straight-line fallback.
- Redesigns Tools and offline preparation around mission/map download, progress save and synchronization.
- Coordinates the player service-worker cache as `saga-player-shell-v516-road-guide-tools`.
- Adds guards for map markers, routing, offline recovery, GPS hardening and Tools UI.
- Validates contracts in Docker, TypeScript/Vite, npm audit and candidate-first deployment.

'''
if not changelog.startswith("# Changelog\n\n"):
    raise SystemExit("ERROR: CHANGELOG inesperado")
changelog = entry + changelog[len("# Changelog\n\n"):]
changelog_path.write_text(changelog, encoding="utf-8")

notes = '''# SAGA Engine v0.5.3 — Offline GPS and field map release

SAGA Engine v0.5.3 focuses on reliability and clarity during real outdoor
missions. It hardens GPS startup and offline recovery, clarifies mission-node
states, introduces an optional road-following route guide and reorganizes the
field Tools experience.

## GPS and map behaviour

- Starts from a fresh GPS reading instead of centring on an old stored position.
- Preserves free map exploration after dragging.
- Uses the compass as a predictable two-state control: mission overview, then return to the player with tracking re-enabled.
- Keeps the player marker stable while location updates arrive.
- Preserves the existing bottom navigation and mobile safe-area behaviour.

## Mission-node semantics

- Completed nodes are green.
- The next active node is yellow/gold and is the only node with an animated halo.
- Future locked nodes are red.
- Every node keeps its route number visible.
- QR nodes use one small type badge for collectible, key/requirement, clue or bonus roles, avoiding duplicate lock symbols.

## Road-following guide

- Requests driving-road geometry from OSRM between mission nodes when online.
- Draws a high-contrast blue guide suitable for satellite maps.
- Connects off-road node positions to the nearest snapped road point when useful.
- Caches successful route geometry locally for later reuse.
- Does not replace a failed route with a misleading straight line.

The public OSRM service is a routing aid, not turn-by-turn navigation. Rural and
mountain missions should be field-tested because the driving profile may prefer
roads rather than walking paths or trails.

## Tools and offline preparation

- Adds a clearer field-centre header in Tools.
- Reorganizes language, field content, GPS and diagnostics into visible sections.
- Replaces the old offline card with a mission-preparation workflow.
- Uses clearer actions for downloading the mission/map, saving progress and synchronizing pending events.
- Coordinates the PWA cache as `saga-player-shell-v516-road-guide-tools`.

## Validation

- Map marker and road-guide guards.
- Offline/GPS hardening and recovery guards.
- Offline Tools UI guard.
- Privacy and protected-files guards.
- Runtime contract checks inside Docker.
- TypeScript and Vite production build.
- npm audit with zero known vulnerabilities.
- Candidate-first Docker deployment and production smoke checks.

## Known follow-up work

- Field-test road routing across urban, rural and mountain missions.
- Add route-profile selection such as driving, cycling or walking when supported.
- Store route geometry directly inside downloadable mission packs.
- Continue tuning QR badges and overlap handling using real mobile screenshots.
- Split the large frontend bundle through dynamic imports and game-level chunks.
'''
Path("RELEASE_NOTES.md").write_text(notes, encoding="utf-8")
print("OK release docs v0.5.3")
